{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FPUUJhN6MXgk12mEHkAkVY","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines review form\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026 - Instruction for Authors\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors\"},{\"title\":\"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026 Conference | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2026%2FConference\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026 - Call for Papers\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl.org/contributions/call-for-papers\"},{\"title\":\"Robot Learning Foundation\",\"url\":\"https://www.robot-learning.org/\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl.org/\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2025 Conference | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2025%2FConference\"},{\"title\":\"Conference on Robot Learning (@corl_conf) / Posts / X\",\"url\":\"https://x.com/corl_conf?lang=en\"},{\"title\":\"ICLR 2026 Reviewer Guide\",\"url\":\"https://iclr.cc/Conferences/2026/ReviewerGuide\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found information related to CoRL 2026, though the specific CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines and review form were not directly returned. Here's what I found:\n\n**CoRL 2026 Conference Information:**\nCoRL 2026 will be held November 9-12, 2026 in Austin, Texas, US, and it is an annual international conference focusing on the intersection of robotics and machine learning.\n\n**Reviewer Requirements:**\nAll submissions must include at least one author who agrees to serve as a CoRL reviewer, and they are qualified if they have at least one accepted publication at a previous robotics (CoRL/ICRA/IROS/RSS) or learning conference (ICLR/NeurIPS/ICML) or equivalent journal.\n\n**Review Process:**\nThe aim is to have at least two reviewers per paper.\n\nThe search results did not return a dedicated page specifically for CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines or the review form itself. For more detailed information about the specific review form and guidelines for CoRL 2026, you may want to check the CoRL 2026 OpenReview page directly at https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org/CoRL/2026/Conference or contact the CoRL 2026 organizers through the official website at corl.org.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01d718a6-ac11-4c69-ac4b-36f76b2791b4","uuid":"0721a488-bafa-4afd-9260-5d3c11f28385","timestamp":"2026-05-13T03:19:55.022Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines review form","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_015ZY498nDg2CeDd9jkWZezm","content":[{"title":"CoRL 2026 - Instruction for Authors","url":"https://www.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors"},{"title":"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023","url":"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines"},{"title":"CoRL 2026 Conference | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2026%2FConference"},{"title":"CoRL 2026 - Call for Papers","url":"https://www.corl.org/contributions/call-for-papers"},{"title":"Robot Learning Foundation","url":"https://www.robot-learning.org/"},{"title":"CoRL 2026","url":"https://www.corl.org/"},{"title":"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews","url":"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews"},{"title":"CoRL 2025 Conference | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2025%2FConference"},{"title":"Conference on Robot Learning (@corl_conf) / Posts / X","url":"https://x.com/corl_conf?lang=en"},{"title":"ICLR 2026 Reviewer Guide","url":"https://iclr.cc/Conferences/2026/ReviewerGuide"}]},"Based on the search results, I found information related to CoRL 2026, though the specific CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines and review form were not directly returned. Here's what I found:\n\n**CoRL 2026 Conference Information:**\nCoRL 2026 will be held November 9-12, 2026 in Austin, Texas, US, and it is an annual international conference focusing on the intersection of robotics and machine learning.\n\n**Reviewer Requirements:**\nAll submissions must include at least one author who agrees to serve as a CoRL reviewer, and they are qualified if they have at least one accepted publication at a previous robotics (CoRL/ICRA/IROS/RSS) or learning conference (ICLR/NeurIPS/ICML) or equivalent journal.\n\n**Review Process:**\nThe aim is to have at least two reviewers per paper.\n\nThe search results did not return a dedicated page specifically for CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines or the review form itself. For more detailed information about the specific review form and guidelines for CoRL 2026, you may want to check the CoRL 2026 OpenReview page directly at https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org/CoRL/2026/Conference or contact the CoRL 2026 organizers through the official website at corl.org."],"durationSeconds":5.507572431000001}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Xd7ave1pDATBq7fnMsJ563","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CoRL 2025 reviewer guidelines review form scoring rubric\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026 - Instruction for Authors\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors\"},{\"title\":\"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines\"},{\"title\":\"2025 Reviewer Guidelines\",\"url\":\"https://neurips.cc/Conferences/2025/ReviewerGuidelines\"},{\"title\":\"CORL 2025 Statistics - Paper Copilot\",\"url\":\"https://papercopilot.com/statistics/corl-statistics/corl-2025-statistics/\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2025 Conference | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2025%2FConference\"},{\"title\":\"Review Form\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform\"},{\"title\":\"ICLR 2025 Reviewer Guide\",\"url\":\"https://iclr.cc/Conferences/2025/ReviewerGuide\"},{\"title\":\"Robot Learning Foundation\",\"url\":\"https://www.robot-learning.org/\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2025 Accepted Paper List - Paper Copilot\",\"url\":\"https://papercopilot.com/paper-list/corl-paper-list/corl-2025-paper-list/\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found some relevant information about CoRL reviewer guidelines. However, the specific CoRL 2025 reviewer guidelines and scoring rubric details are limited in these results. Here's what I found:\n\n## Available Information\n\nThe search results primarily contain information from **CoRL 2023 and CoRL 2024**, as well as some references to CoRL 2026. For **CoRL 2025 specifically**, the OpenReview page exists but doesn't provide detailed content in the search results.\n\n### From CoRL 2023/2024 Guidelines:\n\nCoRL papers are required to include a limitations section, and reviewers should treat honestly reported limitations kindly while pointing out obvious shortcomings or flaws not reported by authors, which should be strongly reflected in scores.\n\nReviewers should be constructive and concrete, courteous and respectful, start with positive aspects, suggest improvements, and accept diverse views.\n\nSubmissions are evaluated based on the significance and novelty of results, either theoretical or empirical.\n\n## Where to Find Complete Guidelines\n\nFor the complete and current CoRL 2025 reviewer guidelines with the detailed review form and scoring rubric, I recommend:\n\n1. Visiting the CoRL 2025 Conference OpenReview homepage\n2. Checking the official CoRL website at corl.org for reviewer instructions\n3. Contacting the CoRL 2025 organizers directly\n\nThe specific scoring scale and detailed rubric for CoRL 2025 was not fully captured in these search results.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01d718a6-ac11-4c69-ac4b-36f76b2791b4","uuid":"3c8e1d33-f878-45df-b333-1d0953aaafc8","timestamp":"2026-05-13T03:19:55.995Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"CoRL 2025 reviewer guidelines review form scoring rubric","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01DMSyTN1aDGind1rr8BBi8C","content":[{"title":"CoRL 2026 - Instruction for Authors","url":"https://www.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors"},{"title":"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023","url":"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines"},{"title":"2025 Reviewer Guidelines","url":"https://neurips.cc/Conferences/2025/ReviewerGuidelines"},{"title":"CORL 2025 Statistics - Paper Copilot","url":"https://papercopilot.com/statistics/corl-statistics/corl-2025-statistics/"},{"title":"CoRL 2025 Conference | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2025%2FConference"},{"title":"Review Form","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform"},{"title":"ICLR 2025 Reviewer Guide","url":"https://iclr.cc/Conferences/2025/ReviewerGuide"},{"title":"Robot Learning Foundation","url":"https://www.robot-learning.org/"},{"title":"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews","url":"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews"},{"title":"CoRL 2025 Accepted Paper List - Paper Copilot","url":"https://papercopilot.com/paper-list/corl-paper-list/corl-2025-paper-list/"}]},"Based on the search results, I found some relevant information about CoRL reviewer guidelines. However, the specific CoRL 2025 reviewer guidelines and scoring rubric details are limited in these results. Here's what I found:\n\n## Available Information\n\nThe search results primarily contain information from **CoRL 2023 and CoRL 2024**, as well as some references to CoRL 2026. For **CoRL 2025 specifically**, the OpenReview page exists but doesn't provide detailed content in the search results.\n\n### From CoRL 2023/2024 Guidelines:\n\nCoRL papers are required to include a limitations section, and reviewers should treat honestly reported limitations kindly while pointing out obvious shortcomings or flaws not reported by authors, which should be strongly reflected in scores.\n\nReviewers should be constructive and concrete, courteous and respectful, start with positive aspects, suggest improvements, and accept diverse views.\n\nSubmissions are evaluated based on the significance and novelty of results, either theoretical or empirical.\n\n## Where to Find Complete Guidelines\n\nFor the complete and current CoRL 2025 reviewer guidelines with the detailed review form and scoring rubric, I recommend:\n\n1. Visiting the CoRL 2025 Conference OpenReview homepage\n2. Checking the official CoRL website at corl.org for reviewer instructions\n3. Contacting the CoRL 2025 organizers directly\n\nThe specific scoring scale and detailed rubric for CoRL 2025 was not fully captured in these search results."],"durationSeconds":6.33501007}}
