requently-asked-questions/"}]},"Based on the search results, I found information about CoRL 2024's instruction for reviews. Submissions will be evaluated based on the significance and novelty of the results, either theoretical or empirical.\n\nThe search results show the review criteria for regular papers, but the specific details about the review form rating scale were not fully included in the snippet from the official instructions page. The first search result indicates there is a full \"Instruction for Reviews\" page on the CoRL 2024 website (2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews), but the rating scale details are not shown in the excerpt provided.\n\nTo get the complete rating scale information, you would need to visit the full instruction page directly at: https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews\n\nWould you like me to search for more specific information about the CoRL 2024 review rating scale, such as whether it uses a numerical scale (e.g., 1-5 or 1-10) and what each rating level represents?"],"durationSeconds":4.6415316189999976}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015Y9Zv3hTFa6x96gKV4G1nt","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CoRL 2023 reviewer guidelines rating scale acceptance criteria\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2023 Accepted Paper List - Paper Copilot\",\"url\":\"https://papercopilot.com/paper-list/corl-paper-list/corl-2023-paper-list/\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2023 Statistics - Paper Copilot\",\"url\":\"https://papercopilot.com/statistics/corl-statistics/corl-2023-statistics/\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl2023.org/\"},{\"title\":\"ICLR 2023 Reviewer Guide\",\"url\":\"https://iclr.cc/Conferences/2023/ReviewerGuide\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL Statistics - Paper Copilot\",\"url\":\"https://papercopilot.com/statistics/corl-statistics/\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2023 Conference | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2023%2FConference\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2025 Accepted Paper List - Paper Copilot\",\"url\":\"https://papercopilot.com/paper-list/corl-paper-list/corl-2025-paper-list/\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 Accepted Paper List - Paper Copilot\",\"url\":\"https://papercopilot.com/paper-list/corl-paper-list/corl-2024-paper-list/\"}]\n\nI found information about CoRL 2023 reviewer guidelines. Based on the official CoRL 2023 Reviewer Guidelines, here's what was specified:\n\n## Review Evaluation Criteria\n\nThe main review part evaluates the originality, quality, clarity, significance, relevance and limitations of the work.\n\nThe guidelines break down these dimensions as follows:\n\n- **Originality**: Reviewers assess whether the problems or methods are new, if the work is a novel combination of well-known techniques (which can be valuable), how this work differs from previous contributions, and whether related work is adequately cited.\n\n- **Quality**: This evaluates whether the submission is technically sound, whether claims are well supported by theoretical analysis or experimental results, whether the methods used are appropriate, whether it's a complete piece of work or work in progress, and whether the authors are careful and honest about evaluating strengths and weaknesses.\n\n- **Clarity**: Reviewers consider whether the submission is clearly written, well organized, and adequately informs the reader.\n\n## Acceptance Philosophy\n\nThe guidelines emphasize that just because a paper beats state-of-the-art does not necessarily mean it must be accepted if it does not provide novel perspectives, insights, or sufficient knowledge advancement.\n\nThe full reviewer guidelines are available at the official CoRL 2023 website at corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01d718a6-ac11-4c69-ac4b-36f76b2791b4","uuid":"a8b7970d-529f-4ffb-90a7-27ce57a06ecd","timestamp":"2026-05-13T03:20:07.867Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"CoRL 2023 reviewer guidelines rating scale acceptance criteria","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01Fg3JuwazRsCWUAFJz6F8D9","content":[{"title":"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023","url":"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines"},{"title":"CoRL 2023 Accepted Paper List - Paper Copilot","url":"https://papercopilot.com/paper-list/corl-paper-list/corl-2023-paper-list/"},{"title":"CoRL 2023 Statistics - Paper Copilot","url":"https://papercopilot.com/statistics/corl-statistics/corl-2023-statistics/"},{"title":"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews","url":"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews"},{"title":"CoRL 2023","url":"https://www.corl2023.org/"},{"title":"ICLR 2023 Reviewer Guide","url":"https://iclr.cc/Conferences/2023/ReviewerGuide"},{"title":"CoRL Statistics - Paper Copilot","url":"https://papercopilot.com/statistics/corl-statistics/"},{"title":"CoRL 2023 Conference | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2023%2FConference"},{"title":"CoRL 2025 Accepted Paper List - Paper Copilot","url":"https://papercopilot.com/paper-list/corl-paper-list/corl-2025-paper-list/"},{"title":"CoRL 2024 Accepted Paper List - Paper Copilot","url":"https://papercopilot.com/paper-list/corl-paper-list/corl-2024-paper-list/"}]},"I found information about CoRL 2023 reviewer guidelines. Based on the official CoRL 2023 Reviewer Guidelines, here's what was specified:\n\n## Review Evaluation Criteria\n\nThe main review part evaluates the originality, quality, clarity, significance, relevance and limitations of the work.\n\nThe guidelines break down these dimensions as follows:\n\n- **Originality**: Reviewers assess whether the problems or methods are new, if the work is a novel combination of well-known techniques (which can be valuable), how this work differs from previous contributions, and whether related work is adequately cited.\n\n- **Quality**: This evaluates whether the submission is technically sound, whether claims are well supported by theoretical analysis or experimental results, whether the methods used are appropriate, whether it's a complete piece of work or work in progress, and whether the authors are careful and honest about evaluating strengths and weaknesses.\n\n- **Clarity**: Reviewers consider whether the submission is clearly written, well organized, and adequately informs the reader.\n\n## Acceptance Philosophy\n\nThe guidelines emphasize that just because a paper beats state-of-the-art does not necessarily mean it must be accepted if it does not provide novel perspectives, insights, or sufficient knowledge advancement.\n\nThe full reviewer guidelines are available at the official CoRL 2023 website at corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines."],"durationSeconds":6.108035152}}
