{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01PnArVFcpPnt27X8N1BbEMQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01CbMGLemWBkKWmY689v1Ncm","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"R2: Novelty + Related Work review","prompt":"You are Reviewer R2 for a CoRL 2026 submission. Your focus is **novelty, significance, and related work**. Produce a detailed, independent review.\n\n## Venue: CoRL 2026\n- Rating scale: 1-10 (10=strong accept, 1=strong reject). Acceptance rate ~30-35%.\n- Criteria: originality, quality, clarity, significance, relevance to robot learning, limitations.\n\n## Paper Summary\nTitle: \"When Does Multivariate Conformal Prediction Help Robot Action Correction? A Systematic Empirical Study\"\n\nThis paper presents ACR-VLA, a pipeline applying multivariate conformal prediction (CP) to VLA action correction. The system has three components: (i) Conformal Geometry Score (CGS) extracting 45D per-DOF features from K=10 flow-matching samples, (ii) Adaptive Conformal Inference (ACI) with self-referential Chunk Overlap Consistency (COC), and (iii) Conformal Residual Module (CRM) for learned action correction. The paper is framed as a systematic empirical study reporting negative results: all three main claims fail pre-registered kill criteria across 11 experiments on LIBERO/LIBERO-Plus.\n\n## Three Claims (all fail):\n1. Per-DOF conformal features enable dimension-selective correction superior to scalar/none.\n2. COC provides reliable self-referential calibration signal.\n3. Inference-time conformal correction provides orthogonal value when stacked on training-time methods.\n\n## Key Negative Results:\n- A3 ablation: removing conformal features → 0.8pp drop, p=0.38 (kill criterion <2pp triggered)\n- A4: Per-DOF vs scalar: 0.3pp difference (noise)\n- COC-success correlation: ρ=0.18 (weak)\n- SRPO stacking: +1.1pp, p=0.29 (not significant)\n- Full pipeline: only +3pp on LIBERO-Plus but -4.2pp on nominal\n- Root cause: K=10 in 7D → Ledoit-Wolf shrinkage 0.91, effective rank 1.3 (covariance degeneracy)\n\n## Stated Contributions:\n1. Systematic negative result with precise covariance diagnostics\n2. COC signal failure mode characterization\n3. Per-perturbation analysis showing augmentation-bounded correction\n\n## Related Work Mentioned:\n- CP for robotics: ReconVLA (scalar nonconformity score), CP-in-the-Loop, UPS\n- Action correction: A2C2, PLD (residual policies without calibrated uncertainty), SAFE (OOD detection)\n- Robustness: RobustVLA, DiG-Flow, SRPO (training-time methods)\n- Multivariate CP: Ledoit-Wolf shrinkage theory\n- References: 10 total (Vovk et al. 2005, Ledoit &amp; Wolf 2004, LIBERO-Plus Kim et al. 2024, ReconVLA Luo et al. 2024, SRPO Ren et al. 2024, Gibbs &amp; Candès 2021, π0 Black et al. 2024, A2C2 Liang et al. 2024, SAFE Dixit et al. 2024, DiG-Flow Wu et al. 2024)\n\n## Your Review Task\nAssess:\n1. **Novelty**: Is the negative result itself novel and surprising? Or is the covariance degeneracy outcome predictable from basic statistics (K=10, p=7 → p/n=0.7)?\n2. **Significance for CoRL**: Do these negative results provide sufficient value for the robot learning community? Is a negative-result empirical study appropriate for CoRL?\n3. **Related work completeness**: Are key baselines and prior works missing? Is the positioning against A2C2/ReconVLA/SRPO fair?\n4. **Framing and narrative**: Is the paper well-framed as an empirical study? Does it avoid burying the lede?\n5. **Writing quality and clarity**.\n6. **Reference quality**: Only 10 references — is this sufficient? Are there important missing citations?\n7. **Contribution granularity**: Are the three \"contributions\" substantial enough individually? Could they have been predicted a priori without running experiments?\n8. **Impact**: Will practitioners change behavior based on these findings?\n\nProduce your review in this format:\n\n### R2 Review: Novelty &amp; Related Work\n\n**Summary** (2-3 sentences)\n\n**Strengths** (numbered list)\n\n**Weaknesses** (numbered list)\n\n**Questions for Authors** (numbered list)\n\n**Missing Related Work or Baselines**\n\n**Minor Issues**\n\n**Scores:**\n- Novelty: X/4\n- Significance: X/4\n- Clarity: X/4\n- Related Work Coverage: X/4\n- Overall (novelty/related work perspective): X/10\n- Confidence: X/5\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2813,"cache_read_input_tokens":62170,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2813},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01d718a6-ac11-4c69-ac4b-36f76b2791b4","uuid":"c3eda495-da76-43fe-b849-b7bb39b8af50"}
